## Component Rules

### Cards

```dart
// Standard card — always use this pattern
Container(
  decoration: BoxDecoration(
    color: Theme.of(context).colorScheme.surface,
    borderRadius: BorderRadius.circular(AppRadius.lg),
    border: Border.all(
      color: Theme.of(context).brightness == Brightness.light
          ? AppColors.borderLight
          : AppColors.borderDark,
      width: 0.5,
    ),
  ),
  padding: const EdgeInsets.all(AppSpacing.lg),
  child: ...,
)
```

Never use Card() widget — it adds elevation and shadow. Use Container with decoration instead.

---

### Option Rows (Test screen)

Three visual states. Always full-width. Never use button shape.

```dart
// Unselected
Container(
  decoration: BoxDecoration(
    color: Theme.of(context).colorScheme.surface,
    borderRadius: BorderRadius.circular(AppRadius.md),
    border: Border.all(color: borderColor, width: 0.5),
  ),
  ...
)

// Selected (before answer revealed)
Container(
  decoration: BoxDecoration(
    color: AppColors.primaryLight, // dark: AppColors.primaryDeep
    borderRadius: BorderRadius.circular(AppRadius.md),
    border: Border.all(color: AppColors.primary, width: 2),
  ),
  ...
)

// Correct answer revealed
Container(
  decoration: BoxDecoration(
    color: isDark ? AppColors.correctBgDark : AppColors.correctBg,
    borderRadius: BorderRadius.circular(AppRadius.md),
    border: Border.all(color: AppColors.correct, width: 2),
  ),
  ...
)

// Wrong answer revealed
Container(
  decoration: BoxDecoration(
    color: isDark ? AppColors.wrongBgDark : AppColors.wrongBg,
    borderRadius: BorderRadius.circular(AppRadius.md),
    border: Border.all(color: AppColors.wrong, width: 2),
  ),
  ...
)
```

Option key badge (A, B, C, D):
- Unselected: gray background, secondary text color
- Selected: AppColors.primary background, white text
- Correct: AppColors.correct background, white text
- Wrong: AppColors.wrong background, white text

