### Question Palette Grid

States for each cell:
- Not visited: surfaceSecondary background, onSurfaceVariant text
- Attempted: correctBg background, correctText text (light) / correctBgDark, correctTextDark (dark)
- Flagged: warningBg background, warningText text (light) / warningBgDark, warningTextDark (dark)
- Current: AppColors.primary background, white text

---

## Dark Mode Rules

**CRITICAL: Never hardcode any color value outside of app_colors.dart.**

Always use one of:
1. `Theme.of(context).colorScheme.surface` — primary surface
2. `Theme.of(context).colorScheme.surfaceContainerLow` — secondary surface
3. `Theme.of(context).colorScheme.onSurface` — primary text
4. `Theme.of(context).colorScheme.onSurfaceVariant` — secondary text
5. `AppColors.X` constants where X has explicit light/dark variants

For colored backgrounds (correct/wrong/info/warning), always check brightness:
```dart
final isDark = Theme.of(context).brightness == Brightness.dark;
final bgColor = isDark ? AppColors.correctBgDark : AppColors.correctBg;
final textColor = isDark ? AppColors.correctTextDark : AppColors.correctText;
```

Text on any colored background must ALWAYS use the matching text constant —
never use onSurface or onSurfaceVariant on colored backgrounds.

---
## Architecture — Clean Architecture

This project follows Clean Architecture strictly. Every feature has three layers:

### Data layer
- Repositories (implementation) — talk to data sources directly
- Data sources — question_db.dart (sqflite), user_db.dart (Drift), PrefsService
- Models — raw data classes with fromJson / fromSqflite / fromDrift constructors
  and toJson / toDrift conversion methods

### Domain layer  
- Entities — pure Dart classes with no Flutter or database dependencies
- Repository interfaces (abstract classes) — define the contract
- Use cases — one class per user action, single execute() method,
  depends only on repository interfaces never implementations

### Presentation layer
- Screens — HookConsumerWidget, no business logic
- Providers — call use cases only, never repositories or data sources directly
- Widgets — dumb, receive data and callbacks only

### Rules
- Dependencies point inward only — presentation → domain ← data
- Domain layer has zero Flutter imports — pure Dart only
- Use cases have one responsibility each — never combine two actions
- Providers never import from the data layer directly
- Repositories are injected via Riverpod providers — never instantiated manually
----

## Database Architecture

### Two separate databases

**1. Question database (read-only)**
- Pre-built SQLite file bundled in `assets/db/upsc_questions.db`
- On first launch, copy from assets to device documents directory using path_provider
- Access via raw sqflite queries — not Drift
- Never write to this database

**2. User database (Drift)**
- Stores: sessions, session_questions, bookmarks, revision_queue
- Located in app documents directory
- All writes go here

---

### Question DB Schema (SQLite — read only)

```sql
CREATE TABLE questions (
  uuid              TEXT PRIMARY KEY,
  subject_slug      TEXT NOT NULL,
  topic_slug        TEXT NOT NULL,
  sub_topic_slug    TEXT NOT NULL,
  correct_option    TEXT NOT NULL,
  question_type     TEXT,
  trap_type         TEXT,
  has_table         INTEGER DEFAULT 0
);

CREATE TABLE question_translations (
  question_uuid         TEXT NOT NULL,
  language              TEXT NOT NULL,
  display_text          TEXT NOT NULL,
  concept_anchor        TEXT,
  final_explanation     TEXT,
  upsc_trap_explanation TEXT,
  strong_distractor     TEXT,
  elimination_logic     TEXT,
  statement_analysis    TEXT,
  concepts_used         TEXT,
  header_text           TEXT,
  footer_text           TEXT,
  columns               TEXT,
  rows                  TEXT,
  PRIMARY KEY (question_uuid, language),
  FOREIGN KEY (question_uuid) REFERENCES questions(uuid)
);

CREATE TABLE topic_translations (
  topic_slug      TEXT NOT NULL,
  subject_slug    TEXT NOT NULL,
  language        TEXT NOT NULL,
  display_name    TEXT NOT NULL,
  PRIMARY KEY (topic_slug, subject_slug, language)
);

CREATE INDEX idx_subject ON questions(subject_slug);
CREATE INDEX idx_topic ON questions(subject_slug, topic_slug);
CREATE INDEX idx_sub_topic ON questions(subject_slug, topic_slug, sub_topic_slug);
CREATE INDEX idx_qt_lang ON question_translations(question_uuid, language);
```

Notes:
- `elimination_logic`, `statement_analysis`, `concepts_used`, `columns`, `rows` are JSON strings
- English is the canonical language — all questions have a `language = 'en'` row in question_translations
- Hindi rows added later when Hindi content is available
- Subject display names are hardcoded in the app (only 6 subjects)
- Topic display names live in topic_translations

---

### Unseen Questions Logic

When generating a test session, prioritise questions the user has never attempted:

```sql
-- Unseen questions for a given subject
SELECT q.uuid FROM questions q
WHERE q.subject_slug = ?
AND q.uuid NOT IN (
  SELECT sq.question_uuid FROM session_questions sq
)
ORDER BY RANDOM()
LIMIT ?;

-- If unseen count < requested count, fill remainder with seen questions
SELECT q.uuid FROM questions q
WHERE q.subject_slug = ?
AND q.uuid IN (
  SELECT sq.question_uuid FROM session_questions sq
)
ORDER BY RANDOM()
LIMIT ?;
```

---

### User DB Schema (Drift)

```dart
// Sessions
class Sessions extends Table {
  TextColumn get id => text()();
  // UUID generated at session creation, primary key

  DateTimeColumn get createdAt => dateTime()();
  DateTimeColumn get completedAt => dateTime().nullable()();

  TextColumn get subjectSlug => text()();
  TextColumn get topicSlug => text().nullable()();
  TextColumn get subTopicSlug => text().nullable()();

  TextColumn get mode => text()();
  // 'exam' | 'learning'

  TextColumn get status => text()();
  // 'in_progress' | 'completed' | 'abandoned'

  IntColumn get questionCount => integer()();
  BoolColumn get isTimed => boolean()();

  IntColumn get timeLimitSecs => integer().nullable()();
  // exam mode: total test time in seconds
  // learning mode: per-question time limit in seconds (45 | 60 | 120)

  TextColumn get language => text().withDefault(const Constant('en'))();

  @override
  Set<Column> get primaryKey => {id};
}

// Session Questions
class SessionQuestions extends Table {
  TextColumn get id => text()();
  // UUID, primary key

  TextColumn get sessionId => text().references(Sessions, #id)();
  TextColumn get questionUuid => text()();

  IntColumn get position => integer()();
  // order within the session, 1-indexed

  TextColumn get selectedOption => text().nullable()();
  // 'a' | 'b' | 'c' | 'd' | null

  BoolColumn get isCorrect => boolean().nullable()();

  TextColumn get status => text().withDefault(const Constant('unattempted'))();
  // 'unattempted' | 'correct' | 'wrong' | 'timed_out'
  // timed_out = counts as unattempted for scoring, NOT wrong

  IntColumn get timeSpentSecs => integer().nullable()();
  BoolColumn get flagged => boolean().withDefault(const Constant(false))();

  @override
  Set<Column> get primaryKey => {id};
}

// Bookmarks
class Bookmarks extends Table {
  TextColumn get id => text()();
  // UUID, primary key

  TextColumn get questionUuid => text()();
  DateTimeColumn get createdAt => dateTime()();
  TextColumn get note => text().nullable()();

  @override
  Set<Column> get primaryKey => {id};
}

// Revision Queue
class RevisionQueue extends Table {
  TextColumn get id => text()();
  // UUID, primary key

  TextColumn get questionUuid => text().unique()();
  // unique — one row per question, never duplicates

  DateTimeColumn get addedAt => dateTime()();

  TextColumn get reason => text()();
  // 'wrong' | 'bookmarked'

  IntColumn get correctStreak => integer().withDefault(const Constant(0))();
  // exits queue when correctStreak >= 2 on separate calendar days

  DateTimeColumn get lastCorrectAt => dateTime().nullable()();
  // used to enforce "separate days" rule

  @override
  Set<Column> get primaryKey => {id};
}
```

---

### Scoring Formula

```dart
// UPSC Prelims: +2 correct, -0.66 wrong, 0 unattempted/timed_out
double calculateNetScore(int correct, int wrong) {
  return (correct * 2) - (wrong * 0.66);
}

// Accuracy — only counts attempted questions (not unattempted or timed_out)
double calculateAccuracy(int correct, int attempted) {
  if (attempted == 0) return 0;
  return (correct / attempted) * 100;
}
```

---

### Shared Preferences Keys

```dart
class PrefKeys {
  static const currentStreak   = 'current_streak';      // int
  static const longestStreak   = 'longest_streak';      // int
  static const lastActiveDate  = 'last_active_date';    // String 'yyyy-MM-dd'
  static const dailyGoal       = 'daily_goal';          // int, default 25
  static const language        = 'language';            // String 'en' | 'hi'
}
```

Daily goal progress is derived at query time:
```sql
SELECT COUNT(*) FROM session_questions sq
JOIN sessions s ON sq.session_id = s.id
WHERE DATE(s.created_at) = DATE('now')
AND sq.status != 'unattempted';
```

---

## State Management (Hooks Riverpod)

### Widget base class rules

- ALWAYS extend `HookConsumerWidget` — never `StatelessWidget`, `StatefulWidget`, or `ConsumerWidget`
- NEVER use `StatefulWidget` — replace all local state with hooks
- The `build` method signature is always: `Widget build(BuildContext context, WidgetRef ref)`

```dart
// CORRECT — always this pattern
class MyScreen extends HookConsumerWidget {
  const MyScreen({super.key});

  @override
  Widget build(BuildContext context, WidgetRef ref) {
    final count = useState(0);
    final controller = useTextEditingController();
    final data = ref.watch(myProvider);
    return ...;
  }
}
```

### Hooks for local UI state

Use flutter_hooks for ALL ephemeral widget-level state. Never use StatefulWidget.

```dart
// Local primitive state
final isExpanded = useState(false);
final selectedIndex = useState(0);

// Controllers — always use hooks, never instantiate manually
final searchController = useTextEditingController();
final scrollController = useScrollController();
final animController = useAnimationController(duration: const Duration(milliseconds: 300));

// Memoised values
final filtered = useMemoized(() => items.where((i) => i.active).toList(), [items]);

// Side effects
useEffect(() {
  // runs once on mount
  return null; // return a cleanup function or null
}, const []);

useEffect(() {
  // runs when dependency changes
  return null;
}, [someDependency]);
```

### Providers — use code generation

```dart
// Async provider (data loading)
@riverpod
Future<List<Question>> subjectQuestions(Ref ref, String subject) async {
  final db = ref.watch(questionDbProvider);
  return db.getQuestionsBySubject(subject);
}

// Sync notifier (complex state with methods)
@riverpod
class TestSessionNotifier extends _$TestSessionNotifier {
  @override
  TestSessionState build() => TestSessionState.initial();

  void selectOption(String questionUuid, String option) {
    state = state.copyWith(...);
  }

  void flagQuestion(String questionUuid) {
    state = state.copyWith(...);
  }
}

// Simple computed value
@riverpod
double netScore(Ref ref, String sessionId) {
  final session = ref.watch(sessionProvider(sessionId));
  return session.correct * 2 - session.wrong * 0.66;
}
```

### Provider placement

- Keep providers in feature folders: `features/test_engine/providers/test_session_provider.dart`
- Core/shared providers in `core/providers/`
- Always use `@riverpod` annotation — never create providers manually without codegen

### Watching vs reading

```dart
// In build() — use watch (rebuilds on change)
final questions = ref.watch(questionsProvider);

// In callbacks / event handlers — use read (no rebuild)
onPressed: () => ref.read(testSessionProvider.notifier).submitTest(),
```

### Never use

- `StateProvider` — use `@riverpod` notifier instead
- `ChangeNotifierProvider` — not compatible with code gen pattern
- `ConsumerWidget` or `ConsumerStatefulWidget` — always use `HookConsumerWidget`
- `StatefulWidget` anywhere in the codebase

