```

---

## Test Modes

### Exam Mode
- All questions shown one at a time
- Tap option to select, tap again or different to change — never locks mid-test
- Previous / Next navigation always available
- Question palette shows attempted / flagged / not visited / current states
- Submit button with confirmation dialog
- Timer counts down total test time (show in top bar)
- No explanation shown during test
- After submit → ResultsScreen with stats only (no explanations in v1)

### Learning Mode
- All questions shown one at a time
- Tap option → answer locks immediately, cannot change
- Per-question countdown timer (45s / 1min / 2min — user configures)
- Timer stops when answer is tapped
- If timer runs out → correct answer revealed, status = 'timed_out' (NOT wrong)
- Explanation card slides up after answer revealed
- "Next question" button appears after explanation
- No going back to previous questions
- No question palette needed

---

## Accuracy Color Rules

Used in history cards, topic lists, subject cards:
- `>= 70%` accuracy → AppColors.correct (green)
- `55–69%` accuracy → AppColors.warning (amber)
- `< 55%` accuracy → AppColors.wrong (red)
- `< 10 attempts` → onSurfaceVariant (muted — data not meaningful yet)
- `0 attempts` → show "—"

---

## Net Score Calculation

UPSC Prelims negative marking: +2 for correct, -0.66 for wrong, 0 for unattempted.

```dart
double calculateNetScore(int correct, int wrong) {
  return (correct * 2) - (wrong * 0.66);
}
```

---

## Session Card Display

History screen session cards show:
- Subject · Topic (if topic test) · Sub-topic (if sub-topic test)
- If subject-only test: show subject name only
- Topic and sub-topic are nullable — render only what exists
- Mode badge: Exam (blue) | Learning (green) | In progress (amber)
- Stats: Accuracy · Score (X/Y) · Net score · Avg time per question
- Completed → "Review" button (outlined)
- In progress → "Resume" button (filled green)

---

## General Flutter Rules

- Never use `Card()` — use `Container` with `BoxDecoration`
- Never hardcode colors — always use `AppColors` or `Theme.of(context).colorScheme`
- Never hardcode font sizes — always use `AppTextStyles`
- Never hardcode spacing — always use `AppSpacing`
- All `ListView` and `SingleChildScrollView` use `physics: const BouncingScrollPhysics()`
- All screens have `SafeArea`
- Use `const` constructors everywhere possible
- Separate business logic from UI — no database calls inside widget `build()` methods
- All async operations show loading state — never leave UI blank while loading
- Handle empty states explicitly — never show empty lists without a message

---

## What NOT to Do

- Do NOT use `StatefulWidget` anywhere — use `HookConsumerWidget` + hooks instead
- Do NOT use `ConsumerWidget` or `ConsumerStatefulWidget` — always `HookConsumerWidget`
- Do NOT use `StateProvider` — use `@riverpod` notifier instead
- Do NOT instantiate controllers manually (TextEditingController(), etc.) — use hooks
- Do NOT use `Card()` widget — use `Container` with `BoxDecoration`
- Do NOT hardcode any Color hex value outside app_colors.dart
- Do NOT use any font other than DM Sans
- Do NOT use FontWeight.w600, w700, w800
- Do NOT call providers directly in build without `ref.watch` / `ref.read`
- Do NOT show explanations in v1 results screen — stats only
- Do NOT add shadow or elevation to any component
- Do NOT use `showDialog` for the question palette — use `showModalBottomSheet`
- Do NOT allow going back to previous questions in Learning mode
- Do NOT mark timed-out questions as wrong — use status 'timed_out', counts as unattempted
